/* Vendor types, as the call sites use them.
 *
 * A type whose members are never touched is an opaque handle and becomes
 * `void *`. A type that gets a designated initializer or a member access
 * becomes a struct carrying exactly the fields that were observed - a
 * `void *` there fails with "initialization of non-aggregate type ... with
 * a designated initializer list", which is what five of the reference
 * codebase's sources did before this distinction existed.
 *
 * Each carries its own guard macro. A typedef cannot be tested with
 * #ifndef the way a macro can, so without one a second declaration of the
 * same name - from another synthesized header, or from a real one that
 * turns up on the include path later - is a hard redefinition error.
 */
